Working through these as straightforward mechanical judgments against the semantic-linefeeds rule (fused → split at sentence end; wrap → rejoin then resplit only at real clause boundaries; don't over-split sentences that fit under ~120 chars; don't push text into a line the window didn't show).

For Unit 6, none of the 11 candidates actually produces the correct 4-sentences/4-lines split without either an unnecessary comma-split or a remaining fused pair — so that one goes to `missing`.

